      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1785642146337,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Record audio and represent as waveform\n\n- Analog to digital: \nAnalog is a continuous signal, and digital consists of discrete values (measurements of the audio).\nSample rate is how many measurements are made by the microphone per second. In Hz.\n.WAV files store this.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Record audio and represent as waveform\n\n- Analog to digital: \nAnalog is a continuous signal, and digital consists of discrete values (measurements of the audio).\nSample rate is how many measurements are made by the microphone per second. In Hz.\n.WAV files store this.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
