    {
      "id": "3EUuriVa4GwszbatI8Y3g",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -2344.036129033259,
      "y": 6549.153921878384,
      "width": 792.5592041015625,
      "height": 240,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#2f9e44",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "cross-hatch",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "dashed",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bovV",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1888877050,
      "version": 1523,
      "versionNonce": 507285923,
      "isDeleted": true,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1785642146337,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Without CNNs, the raw image is uncompressed and required 1 million input features for the linear layer.\nWith CNNs, it's only 625 input layers.\n\nWhat difference does that make?\nBased on values from 1M neurons, the network have to figure out the combinations that equal the\nimage being a dog. Pretty huge task right? If the network only had to look at 625 values to do the\nsame, it is way more manageable.\n\nIn practice this means:\nSlow: During back propagation, all 1M weights have to be tuned.\nOverfittng: Network is too complex (too many parameter) compared to how little data it might be\ntrained on. It'll just memorize the training images instead of learning what a \"dog\" actually looks like.",
      "fontSize": 16,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "containerId": "UqqoiWnrToUwyXhSzSTR-",
      "originalText": "Without CNNs, the raw image is uncompressed and required 1 million input features for the linear layer. With CNNs, it's only 625 input layers.\n\nWhat difference does that make?\nBased on values from 1M neurons, the network have to figure out the combinations that equal the image being a dog. Pretty huge task right? If the network only had to look at 625 values to do the same, it is way more manageable.\n\nIn practice this means:\nSlow: During back propagation, all 1M weights have to be tuned.\nOverfittng: Network is too complex (too many parameter) compared to how little data it might be trained on. It'll just memorize the training images instead of learning what a \"dog\" actually looks like.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
