    },
    {
      "id": "e69SjQAgyrj0GxleWdmnO",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 4229.6094069426235,
      "y": 504.5612837961962,
      "width": 273.095947265625,
      "height": 45,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bqY",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 316042726,
      "version": 886,
      "versionNonce": 1275304259,
      "isDeleted": true,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1785642146338,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Audio and CNNs",
      "fontSize": 36,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Audio and CNNs",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "7Kt8GTQR-om25hYZGmW8D",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 493.52490677390426,
      "y": 576.0979257629464,
      "width": 487.07965087890625,
      "height": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "cross-hatch",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bqZ",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 709147194,
      "version": 213,
      "versionNonce": 445632621,
      "isDeleted": true,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1785642146338,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "We can tweak the CNN layers with the parameters\n- Kernel size\n- Stride\n- Padding",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "We can tweak the CNN layers with the parameters\n- Kernel size\n- Stride\n- Padding",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "pbrExpevZ8ZrOco6yMDnx",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 508.12363449375664,
      "y": 1448.2711183285662,
      "width": 788.4105224609377,
      "height": 200,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "cross-hatch",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bqa",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 76321466,
      "version": 433,
      "versionNonce": 1936029923,
      "isDeleted": true,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1785642146338,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "- Different kernel sizes are specialized for different tasks\n- Large kernels capture broad simple patterns. Helps the network get a quick,\ngeneral understanding of the input before diving into details. Computationally\nexpensive, many parameters.\n- Small kernels: capture fine-grained local details. Using several small filters\ninstead of one big one helps the network learn better. It adds more activation\nsteps (ReLU) in between, which makes it easier to learn complex patterns from\nthe same image area — and it uses fewer parameters too",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "- Different kernel sizes are specialized for different tasks\n- Large kernels capture broad simple patterns. Helps the network get a quick, general understanding of the input before diving into details. Computationally expensive, many parameters.\n- Small kernels: capture fine-grained local details. Using several small filters instead of one big one helps the network learn better. It adds more activation steps (ReLU) in between, which makes it easier to learn complex patterns from the same image area — and it uses fewer parameters too",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "Je47zCvkAK27_nue444oO",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -2633.29935624868,
      "y": 7984.299039674944,
      "width": 258.8879089355469,
      "height": 35,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "cross-hatch",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bqb",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 929362298,
      "version": 1432,
      "versionNonce": 2054503117,
      "isDeleted": true,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1785642146338,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "CNN depth / layers",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "CNN depth / layers",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "q27w4TJTxyU7c_b4jeKZe",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -2631.3532432485417,
      "y": 8046.737935052848,
      "width": 1061.71923828125,
      "height": 75,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "cross-hatch",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bqd",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1020957414,
      "version": 222,
      "versionNonce": 2125096067,
      "isDeleted": true,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1785642146338,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "- In the above examples, one feature map was generated per convolutional layer.\n- A convolutional layer in a neural network does not use just one kernel. It uses many kernels simultaneously.\n- When you use a convolutional layer, you define in and out channels (depth):",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "- In the above examples, one feature map was generated per convolutional layer.\n- A convolutional layer in a neural network does not use just one kernel. It uses many kernels simultaneously.\n- When you use a convolutional layer, you define in and out channels (depth):",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
