      "version": 461,
      "versionNonce": 1481762157,
      "isDeleted": true,
      "boundElements": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "lHD6JjCGHoKwLCGxliZwr"
        }
      ],
      "updated": 1785642146338,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false
    },
    {
      "id": "lHD6JjCGHoKwLCGxliZwr",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -2513.3716812437337,
      "y": 9790.837437871736,
      "width": 531.0595703125,
      "height": 75,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#2f9e44",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "cross-hatch",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "dashed",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bsV",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1270652986,
      "version": 401,
      "versionNonce": 2050700259,
      "isDeleted": true,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1785642146338,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "During training, the network predicts. If it's wrong, an\nerror is sent backward (backpropagation) to adjust\neach kernel slightly to better detect helpful features.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "containerId": "BM9-AIPEHMxfLNBliFNyV",
      "originalText": "During training, the network predicts. If it's wrong, an error is sent backward (backpropagation) to adjust each kernel slightly to better detect helpful features.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "WUBuiBzmNX9Unrpv-uV7L",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -2598.629778054687,
      "y": 14933.529570033465,
      "width": 807.0156860351562,
      "height": 35,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "cross-hatch",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "dashed",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bsW",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 528970042,
      "version": 1373,
      "versionNonce": 1093447629,
      "isDeleted": true,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1785642146338,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "What does it mean to train a convolutional neural network?",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "What does it mean to train a convolutional neural network?",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "CdgMY4BWWFLOBfp7bk46M",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -2600.6105857318457,
      "y": 15014.284210084214,
      "width": 874.6762232918916,
      "height": 350,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "cross-hatch",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bsX",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 903380410,
      "version": 1495,
      "versionNonce": 957398915,
      "isDeleted": true,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1785642146338,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "We train all \"learnable\" parts of the network.\n\nSince a network often has both convolutional layers, linear layers, both of these are\ntrained. Batch norm layers are also trained.\n\nFor CNN layers, two things are trained:\n- Kernels: the numbers inside kernels, the network learns through back propagation. If\nthere are 64 kernels, it learns all 64 sets. They go from random to useful.\n\n- Biases: Each kernel has a bias value, added to every number in its feature map. Bias\nadjusts the feature map importance up or down. E.g. for 64 kernels, the network learns\n64 bias values too.\n\nFor the linear layers, the weights and biases are trained.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "We train all \"learnable\" parts of the network.\n\nSince a network often has both convolutional layers, linear layers, both of these are trained. Batch norm layers are also trained.\n\nFor CNN layers, two things are trained:\n- Kernels: the numbers inside kernels, the network learns through back propagation. If there are 64 kernels, it learns all 64 sets. They go from random to useful.\n\n- Biases: Each kernel has a bias value, added to every number in its feature map. Bias adjusts the feature map importance up or down. E.g. for 64 kernels, the network learns 64 bias values too.\n\nFor the linear layers, the weights and biases are trained.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "v6ZnByC_f6a34F36aSkcw",
